1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,447
One Monday, Arjun was sick.

2
00:00:02,447 --> 00:00:04,952
His cousin did the deliveries instead.

3
00:00:05,252 --> 00:00:08,250
He came at nine, after
the school bus had gone.

4
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,739
Two packs were crushed.

5
00:00:09,739 --> 00:00:11,428
He never said who he was.

6
00:00:11,779 --> 00:00:12,679
Mrs.

7
00:00:12,363 --> 00:00:14,356
Rao called Zoya, upset.

8
00:00:14,706 --> 00:00:16,255
The laddoos were perfect.

9
00:00:16,255 --> 00:00:18,126
The service around them failed.

10
00:00:18,776 --> 00:00:21,183
Laddoo Lab now sells more than a pack.

11
00:00:21,183 --> 00:00:24,186
It sells a weekly delivery,
every Monday morning.

12
00:00:24,536 --> 00:00:26,373
That makes it a service too.

13
00:00:26,373 --> 00:00:28,713
And services are different from things.

14
00:00:29,063 --> 00:00:31,416
You can't touch a service
before you buy it.

15
00:00:31,766 --> 00:00:34,606
It is made at the very
moment it is delivered.

16
00:00:34,956 --> 00:00:38,133
And it changes from day to
day, with the person doing it.

17
00:00:38,783 --> 00:00:40,883
So the 4Ps need some help.

18
00:00:41,183 --> 00:00:47,486
In 1981, Bernard Booms and Mary Jo
Bitner added three more Ps for services.

19
00:00:47,836 --> 00:00:48,736
People.

20
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,430
Everyone the customer meets.

21
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:51,680
Process.

22
00:00:51,453 --> 00:00:55,256
The steps that deliver the
service, the same way every time.

23
00:00:55,606 --> 00:00:56,761
Physical evidence.

24
00:00:56,761 --> 00:01:00,877
What the customer can see and touch,
that shows the service is good.

25
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:03,373
Four plus three makes seven.

26
00:01:03,373 --> 00:01:06,365
The extended marketing mix, or the 7Ps.

27
00:01:07,015 --> 00:01:10,008
Let's replay that Monday,
the old way and the new way.

28
00:01:10,358 --> 00:01:11,318
The old way.

29
00:01:11,318 --> 00:01:12,754
No list, no checks.

30
00:01:12,754 --> 00:01:15,542
The cousin packs in a
hurry and leaves late.

31
00:01:15,892 --> 00:01:18,124
He gets lost, and reaches Mrs.

32
00:01:18,124 --> 00:01:19,427
Rao at nine ten.

33
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:20,781
The bus has gone.

34
00:01:20,781 --> 00:01:22,386
Two packs are crushed.

35
00:01:23,036 --> 00:01:24,284
Now the new way.

36
00:01:24,284 --> 00:01:27,660
On Sunday night, Zoya sends
every family a reminder.

37
00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:30,985
At six, Nani checks each
pack against the list.

38
00:01:31,335 --> 00:01:36,104
At six forty, Arjun leaves with a
route card, wearing his Laddoo Lab cap.

39
00:01:36,454 --> 00:01:40,695
At seven twenty, he hands over
a sealed pack and says his name.

40
00:01:40,695 --> 00:01:41,595
Mrs.

41
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,984
Rao gets a photo message.

42
00:01:43,334 --> 00:01:45,360
That's ten minutes before the bus.

43
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:47,521
Same laddoos, a far better Monday.

44
00:01:48,171 --> 00:01:50,494
Customers don't just buy the product.

45
00:01:50,494 --> 00:01:52,470
They buy the whole experience.

46
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:56,152
Here are all seven Ps around one customer.

47
00:01:56,502 --> 00:02:01,155
The first four, from the last episode:
product, price, place and promotion.

48
00:02:01,505 --> 00:02:02,405
People.

49
00:02:02,119 --> 00:02:06,052
Arjun is trained to be on time,
polite, and to say his name.

50
00:02:06,402 --> 00:02:07,302
Process.

51
00:02:07,107 --> 00:02:11,405
A checklist and a route card, so
every Monday runs the same way.

52
00:02:11,755 --> 00:02:12,965
Physical evidence.

53
00:02:12,965 --> 00:02:16,556
A sealed pack, a clean bag,
and a photo at the door.

54
00:02:16,906 --> 00:02:21,280
These three make an invisible service
easy to see, and easy to trust.

55
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:24,786
Where do we see the
extra Ps at work today?

56
00:02:25,136 --> 00:02:26,036
People.

57
00:02:25,808 --> 00:02:29,533
An airline trains its cabin
crew to stay calm and kind.

58
00:02:29,883 --> 00:02:30,783
Process.

59
00:02:30,602 --> 00:02:34,197
A hospital checks every
patient in the same few steps.

60
00:02:34,547 --> 00:02:35,767
Physical evidence.

61
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:39,139
A bank keeps its branch and
its app clean and clear.

62
00:02:39,489 --> 00:02:40,754
All seven together.

63
00:02:40,754 --> 00:02:43,872
A hotel gets the room
right, and the welcome too.

64
00:02:44,522 --> 00:02:46,817
But more Ps means more to manage.

65
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,394
The good side.

66
00:02:48,394 --> 00:02:53,249
The 7Ps remind us that the experience
matters, not just the product.

67
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:54,747
The hard side.

68
00:02:54,747 --> 00:02:58,341
Training, checks and nicer
packs cost time and money.

69
00:02:58,341 --> 00:03:01,113
And some say the 4Ps already cover this.

70
00:03:01,463 --> 00:03:04,391
Arjun asks, a checklist, just for laddoos?

71
00:03:04,741 --> 00:03:05,717
Nani smiles.

72
00:03:05,717 --> 00:03:06,744
No shortcuts.

73
00:03:06,744 --> 00:03:09,653
Not in the kitchen, and not at the door.

74
00:03:10,003 --> 00:03:10,903
The lesson?

75
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:13,297
Make the service as good as the product.

76
00:03:13,947 --> 00:03:14,899
Quick check.

77
00:03:14,899 --> 00:03:15,799
Mrs.

78
00:03:15,399 --> 00:03:19,050
Rao gets a sealed pack and
a photo message at her door.

79
00:03:19,050 --> 00:03:20,316
Which P is this?

80
00:03:22,216 --> 00:03:23,313
Physical evidence!

81
00:03:23,313 --> 00:03:26,830
Things she can see and touch,
that show the service is good.

82
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:28,442
So, remember.

83
00:03:28,742 --> 00:03:32,783
Services are hard to touch, made as
they are delivered, and they change

84
00:03:32,783 --> 00:03:33,921
from day to day.

85
00:03:34,271 --> 00:03:39,238
Booms and Bitner added three Ps:
people, process and physical evidence.

86
00:03:39,588 --> 00:03:44,226
Together, the 7Ps shape the whole
experience, not just the product.

87
00:03:44,826 --> 00:03:49,113
Next time, we'll look closely at products,
and the different kinds of products

88
00:03:49,113 --> 00:03:50,013
people buy.
